menu "mqjs SKK Japanese input"

choice MQJS_SKK_BUILTIN_DICT
    prompt "Built-in conversion dictionary"
    default MQJS_SKK_DICT_M
    help
        Which SKK-JISYO gets built into the firmware image and read in
        place out of flash rodata (docs/skk-ime-design.md §6.6).

        This is the dictionary a device has with nothing else flashed. A
        bigger one can also be written to the `jisyo` partition at any
        time WITHOUT rebuilding, and skk.open() prefers it — so the
        choice here is really "what should this image fall back to", and
        the largest useful answer is usually not the largest dictionary.

        The build downloads nothing. Point MQJS_SKK_DICT_SOURCE_DIR at a
        directory holding SKK-JISYO.{S,M,ML,L} from
        https://github.com/skk-dev/dict and the build regenerates the
        image with tools/skk_prep.py, which re-sorts into UTF-8 byte
        order and verifies every entry before writing (the EUC-JP sort
        trap, §6.1). Without the sources the build falls back to an
        already-generated components/skk_core/skk_dict.bin, and without
        that it links no dictionary at all — the firmware still builds
        and skk.open() then needs the partition or a file.

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_NONE
    bool "none (partition or file only)"
    help
        No dictionary in the image: -0 KB. skk.open() finds the `jisyo`
        partition, or throws. Right for a device that always has the
        partition flashed — the built-in copy is dead weight there.

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_S
    bool "S — 3,379 headings (image 117 KB)"
    help
        Smallest. Okuri-ari is only 998 entries, so verb and adjective
        conjugation is largely absent. Useful mainly to prove the path
        works with the least flash.

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_M
    bool "M — 8,346 headings (image 303 KB)"
    help
        The default. Enough for everyday nouns; 1,412 okuri-ari entries
        means conjugated forms often miss. The personal dictionary fills
        the gap over time.

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_ML
    bool "ML — 48,750 headings (image 1.86 MB)"
    help
        Where continuous Japanese writing starts to work (4,349
        okuri-ari entries against M's 1,412).

        It does link, but only just: measured 2026-07-29 the image comes
        out at 6,191,264 B against a 6 MB `factory`, i.e. 2% free. That
        is not headroom worth spending — the next feature breaks the
        build, and the fix would be growing `factory`, which is the exact
        edit that moves `storage` and loses every installed app.

        FLASH ML INTO THE `jisyo` PARTITION INSTEAD (README 3.5). Same
        bytes, same speed — it is mmap'd rather than copied either way —
        but it costs the app image nothing and can be replaced without a
        rebuild. Choose it here only for a device that must work with
        nothing but `idf.py flash`.

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_L
    bool "L — 175,790 headings (image 8.07 MB)"
    help
        Does not fit the 6 MB app partition, so choosing it fails the
        build. Listed because the tooling and the host tests support it;
        on a device it belongs in the `jisyo` partition.

endchoice

choice MQJS_SKK_JISYO_DICT
    prompt "Dictionary written to the `jisyo` partition by `idf.py flash`"
    default MQJS_SKK_JISYO_ML
    help
        THIS is where a big dictionary belongs. The partition is mmap'd
        and read in place, exactly like the built-in image, so the search
        is the same speed — but it costs the app image nothing, it can
        hold pine (8.07 MB) which the app partition never could, and it
        can be replaced without rebuilding the firmware.

        Needs MQJS_SKK_DICT_SOURCE_DIR set (the image is generated from
        the SKK-JISYO source) or a prepared components/skk_core/
        skk_jisyo.bin. With neither, the build says so and skips the
        step: `idf.py flash` still works and the device falls back to
        whatever is built in.

        `idf.py flash` then writes ~1.9 MB more, about 9 seconds.
        `idf.py app-flash` does not, and the partition survives it — so
        the day-to-day loop is unaffected.

config MQJS_SKK_JISYO_NONE
    bool "none — leave the partition alone"
    help
        `idf.py flash` does not touch `jisyo`. Whatever was flashed there
        before stays. Use tools: parttool.py write_partition (README 3.5).

config MQJS_SKK_JISYO_M
    bool "M — 8,346 headings (303 KB)"
    help
        The same dictionary the firmware already carries. Pointless
        unless the built-in one is set to `none`.

config MQJS_SKK_JISYO_ML
    bool "ML — 48,750 headings (1.86 MB)"
    help
        The default. 4,349 okuri-ari entries against M's 1,412, which is
        the number that decides whether conjugated verbs and adjectives
        convert — i.e. whether continuous Japanese writing works at all.

config MQJS_SKK_JISYO_L
    bool "L — 175,790 headings (8.07 MB)"
    help
        Everything. Fits the 8.5 MB partition. Two costs: `idf.py flash`
        writes 8 MB (~34 s), and skk.open() spends 826 ms verifying the
        CRC once per app rather than 197 ms. Conversion speed is
        identical — the index is a sampled tree, so it is 6 cache lines
        either way.

endchoice

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_SOURCE_DIR
    string "Directory holding SKK-JISYO.{S,M,ML,L}"
    default ""
    help
        Absolute path, or relative to the project root. Empty means "do
        not regenerate": the build uses components/skk_core/skk_dict.bin
        as it is, whichever dictionary that happens to be, and warns if
        it is missing. That is the default because the source
        dictionaries are large, carry their own licence terms and are
        gitignored.

config MQJS_SKK_DICT_STRIP_ANNOTATIONS
    bool "Strip ';annotation' from candidates"
    default n
    depends on !MQJS_SKK_DICT_NONE
    help
        Drops the explanatory note some entries carry after ';'. Saves
        538 KB on L and almost nothing on M, and the annotations are not
        displayed in v1 anyway. Only has an effect when the image is
        regenerated (MQJS_SKK_DICT_SOURCE_DIR is set).

endmenu
